president biden will be traveling to  saudi arabia in the middle of july and  he's expected to meet with crown prince  mohammed bin salman also known as mbs  who is the de facto ruler of that  kingdom this is the prince that  president biden said he wanted to make a  pariah because of his involvement in the  murder of the washington post columnist  and saudi dissident jamal khashoggi in  2018. but biden's effort to isolate the  prince were a miserable failure no other  world leader joined in shunning the  prince no costs were imposed on saudi  arabia or the house of saud now biden  needs the prince to do him a favor the  price of gas for american consumers is  at record highs in part because of  russia's invasion of ukraine and biden  needs those gas prices to come down  before the midterm elections in the fall  the only person who can do that  is  the ruler of saudi arabia who can open  up the tap and let more crude oil into  the international system and help bring  crises down so it's the prince and not  the president who has the upper hand in  these negotiations what does mbs want  from biden well first he wants an act of  contrition a kind of apology for that  pariah comment and biden is in effect  giving him that by going to saudi arabia  and meeting him the second thing he  wants is an assurance that this nuclear  deal that biden wants to sign with the  iranians who are saudi arabia's great  enemies that that deal will not put at  risk saudi interest that the iranians  will not then be free to bully the  saudis and their arab neighbors and that  if that happens the united states will  double down on protecting the south and  the third thing he wants is reassurance  that the american security umbrella  which has been provided to his family  the house of saud his country for  decades now will remain against all  enemies most of these things that mbs  wants is actually in america's interest  to give there is a big overlap in saudi  interests and american interests so it  should be possible for biden to make the  deal that the prince wants  [Music]
 

